Project Testing PhaseProject Testing Phase – PocketSmart AI: Smart Budget & Recommendation Assistant

The Project Testing Phase is carried out to verify that PocketSmart AI works correctly, reliably, and meets the project requirements. Each module is tested individually and then tested together as a complete system.

1. Testing Objectives

Identify and fix errors.

Verify that all features work correctly.

Check the accuracy of expense and budget calculations.

Ensure recommendations are generated properly.

Check database operations and data security.

Ensure the application is easy to use.


2. Types of Testing

1. Unit Testing
Each module, such as login, expense entry, and budget calculation, is tested separately.

2. Integration Testing
Checks whether the frontend, backend, database, and recommendation engine work correctly together.

3. Functional Testing
Verifies important functions such as adding expenses, setting budgets, and generating reports.

4. Usability Testing
Checks whether users can easily navigate and use the application.

5. Performance Testing
Checks the application's response time and performance when handling multiple transactions.

3. Sample Test Cases

Test Case	Expected Result

User login with valid details	Login successful
Add a new expense	Expense saved successfully
Set monthly budget	Budget displayed correctly
Add expense above budget	Warning/recommendation displayed
Delete transaction	Transaction removed
View expense chart	Correct chart displayed
Generate recommendation	Suitable recommendation displayed


4. Error Handling

Errors such as invalid input, missing information, incorrect amounts, and database failures are identified and handled appropriately.

5. Final Testing Result

After testing and fixing identified errors, the PocketSmart AI system is verified to provide accurate expense tracking, budget monitoring, financial analysis, and personalized recommendations.
